# Canonical author identities. `git` applies this to log, shortlog and blame
# output, so it corrects attribution retroactively without rewriting history.
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped:
#   - Robb Walters' agent-N@2amlogic.com identities. Those are Loom's own
#     autonomous agents committing under the operator's name; folding them into
#     the human identity would erase the human/agent distinction, which is a
#     policy call rather than a typo.
#   - Joseph Perla <jperla@...>, a different person who shares a first name.

# Two addresses, and one of them carried the wrong surname from a machine's
# leftover git config.
Joseph Turian <turian@gmail.com> <joseph@2amlogic.com>

# A shell `echo` leaked into this machine's user.email, appending "echo" to the
# address on 31 commits. Same identity, malformed address.
Loom Worker <loom-reviewer@users.noreply.github.com> <loom-reviewer@users.noreply.github.comecho>
